# Frontend conventions

These rules apply **everywhere** frontend code lives: `apps/web`, `@repo/ui`, `@repo/auth`, and any other package with React/TS UI. Same naming and modularity — no package exceptions.

## Placement

- Shared atoms/molecules → `@repo/ui`
- Auth UI/client → `@repo/auth`
- App shell / routes / providers → `apps/web/src` (flat — **no** `src/app/` folder)
- Domain UI → `apps/web/src/modules/<moduleName>/` (never `features/`)
- Never reverse-import across modules

## Naming (hard)

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| **Folders** | camelCase only | `projectCard/`, `createProjectForm/` |
| **Components** (files) | PascalCase | `ProjectCard.tsx`, `CreateProjectForm.tsx` |
| **Hooks** (files) | `use` + PascalCase | `useProjectsQuery.ts`, `useDebouncedValue.ts` |
| **Functions / utils** (files) | camelCase | `computeDashboardStats.ts`, `fetchAllTranslations.ts` |

Do **not** use kebab-case for folders or source files (`project-card`, `use-projects-query` = fail).

## Component categories (hard)

Under each module’s `components/`, group units by kind so they are easy to find:

```
modules/<moduleName>/components/
  forms/      # reusable field+submit UI (never only inside a modal file)
  cards/      # list/summary cards
  modals/     # dialogs & modals (shell + open state; compose forms)
  panels/     # page sections / tab bodies
  tables/     # table/row presentation
  layouts/    # shell chrome, page containers (when needed)
```

Add a new category folder only when a clear kind appears (e.g. `charts/`). Do not dump unrelated units at the `components/` root.

Example: `components/forms/createProjectForm/CreateProjectForm.tsx`  
Example: `components/modals/createProjectModal/CreateProjectModal.tsx`

## Forms vs dialogs (hard)

- **Forms are always their own components** under `components/forms/`
- Dialogs / modals live under `components/modals/` and **compose** forms — open state, title, shell only
- Never embed form fields + submit logic only inside a modal file
- Same form must be reusable outside a dialog (page, drawer, wizard step)

## Multi-step flows (hard)

- Use a shared **`useFlowWizard`** hook + **`FlowWizard`** shell — do not invent one-off wizard state machines per feature
- Steps are declared as `{ id, validate? }`; **step UI is standalone forms** selected by `wizard.stepId`
- Feature modules compose flows by wiring forms into the generic wizard — forms stay reusable outside that flow
- Put finish/submit side effects in `onComplete`, not inside the generic hook

## Unit layout

- Prefer flat units inside a category: `components/cards/projectCard/ProjectCard.tsx`
- Domain **cards/panels** that look like cards must use `@repo/ui` `Card` (and related slots) — do not reinvent with ad-hoc `unolio-card` / raw bordered divs
- Add `hooks/`, `utils/`, `types/`, `constants/` **only when that unit has several files**
- Do **not** wrap every file in an empty `component/` ceremony folder
- Shared app helpers → `apps/web/src/hooks/`, `utils/`, `types/` (not `src/app/`)

## Modularity

- **Pages** stay thin (routing, layout, compose)
- **Stateful logic** → hooks (`useX`)
- **Stateless logic** → utils (pure functions)
- Extract reusable UI into sibling components; avoid god-panels that own fetch + filter + dialogs + table

## Stack mandates

- Data: TanStack Query
- Forms: TanStack Form
- Tables: TanStack Table
- Routing: React Router 7+ with the **route config** API (see below)
- Styling: Tailwind + `@repo/ui` tokens
- Copy: i18n keys only (`@repo/i18n` / `react-i18next`)

## Routing (hard)

Use the current React Router route-module API — **not** legacy JSX `<Routes>` / `<Route>` trees or ad-hoc `BrowserRouter` route tables.

Declare routes in a `routes.ts` (or equivalent) via `@react-router/dev/routes`:

```ts
import {
  type RouteConfig,
  route,
  layout,
  index,
  prefix,
} from "@react-router/dev/routes";

export default [
  layout("./modules/marketing/layout.tsx", [
    index("./modules/marketing/pages/homePage/HomePage.tsx"),
    route("contact", "./modules/marketing/pages/contactPage/ContactPage.tsx"),
  ]),
  ...prefix("projects", [
    index("./modules/projects/pages/projectsPage/ProjectsPage.tsx"),
    layout("./modules/projects/layouts/projectLayout.tsx", [
      route(":projectId", "./modules/projects/pages/projectDetailPage/ProjectDetailPage.tsx"),
      route(":projectId/edit", "./modules/projects/pages/editProjectPage/EditProjectPage.tsx"),
    ]),
  ]),
] satisfies RouteConfig;
```

- Prefer `layout`, `index`, `route`, and `prefix` composition over nested JSX route trees
- Route **module file paths** still follow our naming rules (camelCase folders, PascalCase components)
- Auth gates belong in layout route modules (`RequireAuth` / `requireRole`), not scattered per page
- Declare routes in `apps/web/src/routes.ts` (SPA: `react-router.config.ts` with `ssr: false`, `appDirectory: "src"`)
- Do not introduce new JSX `<Routes>` / `<Route>` maps for production routing (tests may mirror the tree via route objects)

## Quality

- No business logic in React pages
- Preserve CSP meta and `sourcemap: false` in production Vite config
- Same-origin `/api` proxy in dev — do not invent cross-origin cookie setups
- Axe smoke must stay green on auth forms
- Clear private React Query caches on login/logout/register/identity-changing refresh (via `@repo/auth` lifecycle — do not import module query keys into auth)
- Destructive UI actions (bulk delete / delete-by-key) require confirmation and must call ownership-aware APIs
- Clients that need complete list datasets must walk `nextCursor` until null; never export a truncated page as complete
